{
  "id": "asoxSchedAlrtQue",
  "name": "sched-alert-queue",
  "active": true,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## sched-alert-queue (alert queue scheduler, N8N-1.4)\n**Trigger:** every 5 s.\n**Inputs:** the Data Tables `asox_alert_queue` and `asox_queue_slots`; lib-config `alert_queue` (only read when the queue has rows).\n**Actions taken:** with nothing pending or running, stops at once (and the run is not saved). Otherwise: requeues `running` rows older than `running_timeout_s` (or fails and parks them after `max_attempts`), deletes `done` rows older than `keep_done_h`, takes a free slot (compare-and-set on the slot's `claim`, read back), claims the oldest pending row (FIFO by row id; compare-and-set `pending` -> `running` with a new token, read back), runs **lib-alert-queue-drain** for that row and waits, then frees the slot. Losing either compare-and-set ends the run: the next tick tries again. At most `alert_queue.slots` rows run at once, because each run holds one slot; with every slot held a tick does nothing.\n**Systems changed:** n8n's own Data Tables (the playbook changes TheHive).\n**Approval:** not applicable.\n**Owner:** n8n.\nSaved: failed runs only. The work is recorded in lib-alert-queue-drain's executions (saved), so the 17,000 idle ticks a day keep nothing.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 560
      },
      "id": "f0a75332-5bb6-5e45-99f4-b98ee99b6e73",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
